{"id": "section-body-03503", "title": "Neonatal Tetanus", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Bacterial Infections", "Neonatal Tetanus"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-03503", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Neonatal Tetanus", "runs": [{"text": "Neonatal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Tetanus"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1802"}}, {"id": "body-03504", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A neuromuscular toxin-mediated illness caused by the anaerobic spore-forming soil bacterium Clostridium tetani. The disease is transmitted when spores enter open wounds (injections, cutting the umbilical cord) or breaks in the skin. While tetanus may occur in adults, infection primarily affects newborns. Incubation period is 3 to 21 days, with an average of approximately 6 days. Usually occurs through introduction of tetanus spores via the umbilical cord during delivery through the use of an unclean instrument to cut the cord, or after delivery by “dressing” the umbilical stump with substances heavily contaminated with tetanus spores.", "runs": [{"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "neuromuscular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "toxin-mediated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "illness"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "anaerobic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spore-forming"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "soil"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bacterium"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Clostridium"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tetani."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disease is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "transmitted"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "when"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spores"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "enter"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "open"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "wounds"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(injections,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cutting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "umbilical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cord)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "breaks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "skin."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "While"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tetanus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may occur in adults, infection primarily affects newborns. Incubation period is 3 to 21 days, with an average of approximately 6 days."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occurs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "through"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "introduction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tetanus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spores"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "via"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "umbilical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cord"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "during"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "delivery"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "through"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "use"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "unclean instrument to cut the cord, or after delivery by “dressing” the umbilical stump with substances heavily contaminated with tetanus spores."}]}, {"id": "body-03506", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Diagnostic Criteria", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Diagnostic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Criteria"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03507", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Sudden inability of a newborn to suck/feed between 2nd and 28th day after birth", "runs": [{"text": "Sudden"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inability"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "newborn"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suck/feed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "between"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2nd"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "28th"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "day"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "birth"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1788"}}, {"id": "body-03508", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Generalized stiffness", "runs": [{"text": "Generalized"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stiffness"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1788"}}, {"id": "body-03509", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Convulsions", "runs": [{"text": "Convulsions"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1788"}}, {"id": "body-03511", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Laboratory Investigation", "runs": [{"text": "Laboratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Investigation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03512", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Diagnosis is mainly clinical as there are no reliable laboratory tests for confirming tetanus", "runs": [{"text": "Diagnosis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mainly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "there"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "no"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reliable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laboratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tests"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "confirming"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tetanus"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1788"}}, {"id": "body-03513", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Blood counts and blood chemical findings are unremarkable.", "runs": [{"text": "Blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "counts"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chemical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "findings"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "unremarkable."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1788"}}, {"id": "body-03514", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Peripheral leukocytosis may be suggestive", "runs": [{"text": "Peripheral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leukocytosis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suggestive"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1788"}}, {"id": "body-03515", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Prevention", "runs": [{"text": "Prevention"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03516", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Immunize women of reproductive age with TTCV, either during pregnancy or outside of pregnancy. This protects the mother and also her baby through the transfer of tetanus antibodies to the fetus.", "runs": [{"text": "Immunize"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "women"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reproductive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "age"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "TTCV,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "either"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "during"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pregnancy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "outside"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pregnancy."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "This"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "protects"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the mother and also her baby through the transfer of tetanus antibodies to the fetus."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1788"}}, {"id": "body-03517", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Good hygienic practices when the mother is delivering a child are also important to prevent neonatal and maternal tetanus.", "runs": [{"text": "Good hygienic practices when the mother is delivering a child are also important to prevent neonatal and maternal "}, {"text": "tetanus."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1788"}}, {"id": "body-03518", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "To be protected throughout life, WHO recommends that an individual receives 6 doses (3 primaries plus 3 booster doses) of TTCV through routine immunization.", "runs": [{"text": "To be protected throughout life, WHO recommends that an individual receives 6 doses (3"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primaries plus 3 booster doses) of TTCV through routine immunization."}]}, {"id": "body-03520", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03521", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Rigorously cleanse the umbilical stump to stop the production of toxin at the site of infection", "runs": [{"text": "Rigorously"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cleanse"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "umbilical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stump"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stop"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "production"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "toxin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "site"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection"}]}, {"id": "body-03523", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03525", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "For Paediatrics", "runs": [{"text": "For"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Paediatrics"}]}, {"id": "body-03526", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "B: amoxicillin + clavulanic acid (PO) via NGT 20–30mg/kg/day divided 8hourly for 7days", "runs": [{"text": "B:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "amoxicillin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "+"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "clavulanic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "via"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "NGT"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "20–30mg/kg/day"}, {"text":